#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179451 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d5ee41f2-7116-52f4-b1f7-923997d994ab" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Double Sum Over a Rectangular Partition Using a Difference of Squares"}] :question/id #uuid "500e1ff1-1a58-57f5-8d85-32ff78dafb35" :question/math-academy-id "e-6117" :question/problem "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- $P_1 = \\left\\{x_0, x_1, \\ldots, x_m\\right\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[4, 6]$\n\n- $P_2 = \\left\\{y_0, y_1, \\ldots, y_n\\right\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[2, 6]$\n\nCalculate  $\\displaystyle\\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n (x_i + x_{i-1})\\Delta x_i \\Delta y_j,$ where $\\Delta x_i = x_i - x_{i-1}$ and $\\Delta y_j = y_j - y_{j-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the product rule, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^m (x_i + x_{i-1})\\Delta x_i \\cdot \\sum_{j=1}^n \\Delta y_j.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^n\\Delta y_j$ is just the length of the interval $[2, 6].$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}=6-2=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the sum over $i,$ we can evaluate it as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})Δ{x}_{1}+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})Δ{x}_{2}+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})Δ{x}_{m} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}\\,+\\,{x}_{0})({x}_{1}\\,-\\,{x}_{0})+({x}_{2}\\,+\\,{x}_{1})({x}_{2}\\,-\\,{x}_{1})+({x}_{m}\\,+\\,{x}_{m-1})({x}_{m}\\,-\\,{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})+({x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{m-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}}-{x}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}^{2}+{x}_{m}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={6}^{2}-{4}^{2} \\\\  & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we finally arrive at \n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^m (x_i + x_{i-1})\\Delta x_i \\cdot \\sum_{j=1}^n\\Delta y_j = 20\\cdot 4 = 80.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179514 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f913fab-d0b5-5e9e-b292-039afe4a148c" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Double Sum Over a Rectangular Partition"}] :question/id #uuid "e2f01953-2fb1-5ddb-83ae-5d8a73e7f7ac" :question/math-academy-id "e-9482" :question/problem "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- $P_1 = \\left\\{x_0, x_1, \\ldots, x_m\\right\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[-1, 2]$\n\n- $P_2 = \\left\\{y_0, y_1, \\ldots, y_n\\right\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[2, 3]$\n\nCalculate $\\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n {3} \\Delta x_i \\Delta y_j,$ where $\\Delta x_i = x_i - x_{i-1}$ and $\\Delta y_j = y_j - y_{j-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple and product rules, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}3Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =3{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & =3{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $\\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^m\\Delta x_i$ and $\\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^n\\Delta y_j$ are just the lengths of the intervals $[-1, 2]$ and $[2,3]$ respectively. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i} & =2-(-1)=3, \\\\ {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j} & =3-2=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we have\n\n$$\n3 \\sum_{i=1}^m \\Delta x_i \\sum_{j=1}^n \\Delta y_j = 3 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 1 = 9.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179910 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f913fab-d0b5-5e9e-b292-039afe4a148c" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Double Sum Over a Rectangular Partition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a56efb23-4fb8-51bc-b762-55181a3cb253" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177461} {:answer/id #uuid "09973326-24c2-52cb-bec5-3ec0b52b6c90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177462} {:answer/id #uuid "3941c435-42fa-52d2-bf17-be580fd5055e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177463} {:answer/id #uuid "3b076f26-a20f-5937-9362-6f275778ef81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177464} {:answer/id #uuid "3b2efd7e-9334-5697-85e2-5c5353caacf2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177465}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a56efb23-4fb8-51bc-b762-55181a3cb253" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177461} :answer-field/id #uuid "3dfdd3f4-2382-5b16-b34f-62244e473bdf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177460}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7cb18f0a-5793-5799-850f-ef66cbf9de18" :question/math-academy-id "q-122867" :question/problem "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- ${P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}}$ is a partition of the interval $[0,2]$\n\n- ${P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}}$ is a partition of the interval $[1,6]$\n\nCalculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j},$ where $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the product rule, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}$ and ${\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}$ are just the lengths of the intervals $[0,2]$ and $[1,6]$ respectively. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i} & =2-0=2, \\\\ {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j} & =6-1=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we have\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}=2\\cdot 5=10.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378066 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f913fab-d0b5-5e9e-b292-039afe4a148c" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Double Sum Over a Rectangular Partition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20c0b6fc-b6db-5230-aa90-eb50213f2c4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378068} {:answer/id #uuid "21057187-cafd-5c3e-a3d3-a501a456f965" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378069} {:answer/id #uuid "68f338e0-bea6-5944-b877-d87fc787d930" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378070} {:answer/id #uuid "0c27b782-5755-5cda-8529-8f10bd09cbd3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378071} {:answer/id #uuid "7581a87c-2cc7-5af3-91dd-749cec688ab4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378072}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20c0b6fc-b6db-5230-aa90-eb50213f2c4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378068} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0bfa80e-5c71-56e7-b4b1-c5ce3d764331" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378067}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "dbeaa7fe-8be4-5956-b251-01b99a5c3c36" :question/math-academy-id "q-123069" :question/problem "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- ${P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}}$ is a partition of the interval $[0,3]$\n\n- ${P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}}$ is a partition of the interval $[4,8]$\n\nCalculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j},$ where $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the product rule, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}$ and ${\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}$ are just the lengths of the intervals $[0,3]$ and $[4,8]$ respectively. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i} & =3-0=3, \\\\ {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j} & =8-4=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we have\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}=3\\cdot 4=12.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378073 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d5ee41f2-7116-52f4-b1f7-923997d994ab" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Double Sum Over a Rectangular Partition Using a Difference of Squares"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de1783a7-57ac-5755-a0c8-bbeaf0a6011d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378075} {:answer/id #uuid "4c276730-1b3a-5e07-bc1e-0ce9710e2c96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378076} {:answer/id #uuid "3526e92a-7a16-5f62-b867-7f493880e8af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378077} {:answer/id #uuid "5c949722-1e7d-5792-970b-9445d731d798" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378078} {:answer/id #uuid "c2046a9f-354a-546f-a30e-e03854ddcf6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378079}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c2046a9f-354a-546f-a30e-e03854ddcf6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378079} :answer-field/id #uuid "631a65c7-7138-5408-ba99-f41d1302f22b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378074}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "945caca7-f42a-5f31-ae86-c966bd57d4f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-123104" :question/problem "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- ${P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}}$ is a partition of the interval $[-1,1]$\n\n- ${P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}}$ is a partition of the interval $[-1,1]$\n\nCalculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}10({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j},$ where $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple and product rules, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n10{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}\\cdot {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}$ is just the length of the interval $[-1,1].$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}=1-(-1) & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the sum over $j,$ we evaluate it as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{j} & =({y}_{1}+{y}_{0})Δ{y}_{1}+({y}_{2}+{y}_{1})Δ{y}_{2}+⋯+({y}_{n}+{x}_{n-1})Δ{y}_{n} \\\\  & =({y}_{1}\\,+\\,{y}_{0})({y}_{1}\\,-\\,{y}_{0})\\,+\\,({y}_{2}\\,+\\,{y}_{1})({y}_{2}\\,-\\,{y}_{1})\\,+\\,⋯\\,+\\,({y}_{n}\\,+\\,{y}_{n-1})({y}_{n}\\,-\\,{y}_{n-1}) \\\\  & =({y}_{1}^{2}-{y}_{0}^{2})+({y}_{2}^{2}-{y}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({y}_{n}^{2}-{y}_{n-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{y}_{1}^{2}}-{y}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{y}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{y}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({y}_{n}^{2}-\\cancel{{y}_{n-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{y}_{0}^{2}+{y}_{n}^{2} \\\\  & ={y}_{n}^{2}-{y}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={1}^{2}-(-1)^{2} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we finally arrive at\n\n$$\n10{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}\\cdot {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{j}.=10\\cdot 2\\cdot 0=0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378080 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f913fab-d0b5-5e9e-b292-039afe4a148c" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Double Sum Over a Rectangular Partition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c3f62adf-e17f-56fe-a9cf-f8819012fb40" :answer/type {:db/ident 