ntervals $[2,3]$ and $[3,8]$ respectively. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i} & =3-2=1, \\\\ {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j} & =8-3=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we have\n\n$$\n4{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}=4\\cdot 1\\cdot 5=20.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378087 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d5ee41f2-7116-52f4-b1f7-923997d994ab" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Double Sum Over a Rectangular Partition Using a Difference of Squares"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2df7bd4b-9fbb-5d05-959c-50e8ca2048f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378089} {:answer/id #uuid "8a5b1c81-d3df-5121-ac23-82ff8a9510bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378090} {:answer/id #uuid "0f8a5b4b-138f-5228-bf85-4b42fd5d0dea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378091} {:answer/id #uuid "2d066937-2c4a-5e6e-889e-a70d7760bdd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "96" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378092} {:answer/id #uuid "88e08c79-f188-5d52-a09b-29e785491666" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378093}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2df7bd4b-9fbb-5d05-959c-50e8ca2048f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378089} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac53f04e-3c07-5ae4-804a-c97cbd11393b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378088}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1b4ef090-1288-5ca1-833a-7ba30aaefd89" :question/math-academy-id "q-149629" :question/problem "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- ${P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}}$ is a partition of the interval $[2,6]$\n\n- ${P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}}$ is a partition of the interval $[4,6]$\n\nCalculate  ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j},$ where $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the product rule, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}\\cdot {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}$ is just the length of the interval $[4,6].$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}=6-4=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the sum over $i,$ we can evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})Δ{x}_{1}+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})Δ{x}_{2}+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})Δ{x}_{n} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})({x}_{m}-{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})+({x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{m-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}}-{x}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}^{2}+{x}_{m}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={6}^{2}-{2}^{2} \\\\  & =32\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we finally arrive at\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}\\cdot {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}=32\\cdot 2=64.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378094 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d5ee41f2-7116-52f4-b1f7-923997d994ab" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Double Sum Over a Rectangular Partition Using a Difference of Squares"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8bcdcdab-6a3d-51c9-b646-fc5e1dfb60e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378096} {:answer/id #uuid "8c082e81-1654-51dc-8778-8fcaafabc4a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378097} {:answer/id #uuid "d2d420d7-1509-52a8-8add-399fc7cfae7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378098} {:answer/id #uuid "5d1ab82b-7f8c-5159-97b9-958ad52a34d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378099} {:answer/id #uuid "f48f8907-a564-5505-98fb-e78ea256bc03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378100}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2d420d7-1509-52a8-8add-399fc7cfae7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378098} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb825214-367e-52a5-af2c-dd696103f49c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378095}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2158d2cd-7cd8-538d-82a4-737072fa1c54" :question/math-academy-id "q-149631" :question/problem "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- ${P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}}$ is a partition of the interval $[3,5]$\n\n- ${P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}}$ is a partition of the interval $[-1,2]$\n\nCalculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j},$ where $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the product rule, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}\\cdot {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}$ is just the length of the interval $[3,5].$ So, we have\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}=5-3=2.\n$$\n\nFor the sum over $j,$ we evaluate it as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{j} & =({y}_{1}+{y}_{0})Δ{y}_{1}+({y}_{2}+{y}_{1})Δ{y}_{2}+⋯+({y}_{n}+{x}_{n-1})Δ{y}_{n} \\\\  & =({y}_{1}+{y}_{0})({y}_{1}-{y}_{0})+({y}_{2}+{y}_{1})({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})+⋯+({y}_{n}+{x}_{n-1})({y}_{n}-{y}_{n-1}) \\\\  & =({y}_{1}^{2}-{y}_{0}^{2})+({y}_{2}^{2}-{y}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({y}_{n}^{2}-{y}_{n-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{y}_{1}^{2}}-{y}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{y}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{y}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({y}_{n}^{2}-\\cancel{{y}_{n-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{y}_{0}^{2}+{y}_{n}^{2} \\\\  & ={y}_{n}^{2}-{y}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={2}^{2}-(-1)^{2} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we finally arrive at \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}\\cdot {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{j}=2\\cdot 3=6.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378101 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d5ee41f2-7116-52f4-b1f7-923997d994ab" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Double Sum Over a Rectangular Partition Using a Difference of Squares"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80bd9d3f-b7bf-5f59-81ef-344217dedd16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378103} {:answer/id #uuid "36b1ed81-0ddf-54a5-acf7-7ab32b3d45fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378104} {:answer/id #uuid "8f5c199a-5e17-5385-a29d-00608a1bf425" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378105} {:answer/id #uuid "85fa8e94-3dd8-592d-acc8-de43bfacefa4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378106} {:answer/id #uuid "808bc833-1d76-5d01-bc0c-6fb6c5179f73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378107}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "80bd9d3f-b7bf-5f59-81ef-344217dedd16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378103} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e7ec25a-087f-509c-b2a9-3bfdb9be9f6a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378102}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4cb6dc3e-d65f-5a78-889b-bf2893192b18" :question/math-academy-id "q-149634" :question/problem "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- ${P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}}$ is a partition of the interval $[2,7]$\n\n- ${P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}}$ is a partition of the interval $[-3,-2]$\n\nCalculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}4({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j},$ where $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple and product rules, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n4{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}\\cdot {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}$ is just the length of the interval $[2,7].$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}=7-2 & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the sum over $j,$ we evaluate it as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{j} & =({y}_{1}+{y}_{0})Δ{y}_{1}+({y}_{2}+{y}_{1})Δ{y}_{2}+⋯+({y}_{n}+{x}_{n-1})Δ{y}_{n} \\\\  & =({y}_{1}\\,+\\,{y}_{0})({y}_{1}\\,-\\,{y}_{0})\\,+\\,({y}_{2}\\,+\\,{y}_{1})({y}_{2}\\,-\\,{y}_{1})\\,+\\,⋯\\,+\\,({y}_{n}\\,+\\,{y}_{n-1})({y}_{n}\\,-\\,{y}_{n-1}) \\\\  & =({y}_{1}^{2}-{y}_{0}^{2})+({y}_{2}^{2}-{y}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({y}_{n}^{2}-{y}_{n-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{y}_{1}^{2}}-{y}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{y}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{y}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({y}_{n}^{2}-\\cancel{{y}_{n-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{y}_{0}^{2}+{y}_{n}^{2} \\\\  & ={y}_{n}^{2}-{y}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =(-2)^{2}-(-3)^{2} \\\\  & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we finally arrive at\n\n$$\n4{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}\\cdot {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{j}=4\\cdot 5\\cdot (-5)=-100.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378108 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d5ee41f2-7116-52f4-b1f7-923997d994ab" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Double Sum Over a Rectangular Partition Using a Difference of Squares"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "50342f8c-5817-58d9-b183-89df4ae186f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-54" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378110} {:answer/id #uuid "fb3d1053-437d-5056-aaf8-c5647d3d89cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378111} {:answer/id #uuid "f803a49e-8f89-5b07-aa7d-b449fe539ff6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378112} {:answer/id #uuid "c45147b2-7c43-5aec-829c-75f029c7f626" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378113} {:answer/id #uuid "06425ad5-3904-50c1-a003-4f1745ffca30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "54" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378114}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c45147b2-7c43-5aec-829c-75f029c7f626" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378113} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd031717-924c-53a1-906f-5f362af89b01" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378109}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "41d30f3a-6e37-555f-9aae-459b7e89604b" :question/math-academy-id "q-149635" :question/problem "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- ${P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}}$ is a partition of the interval $[-4,-1]$\n\n- ${P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}}$ is a partition of the interval $[8,9]$\n\nCalculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}-3({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j},$ where $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple and product rules, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n-3{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}\\cdot {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}$ is just the length of the interval $[8,9].$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}=9-8 & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the sum over $i,$ we evaluate it as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})Δ{x}_{1}+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})Δ{x}_{2}+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})Δ{x}_{n} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}\\,+\\,{x}_{0})({x}_{1}\\,-\\,{x}_{0})\\,+\\,({x}_{2}\\,+\\,{x}_{1})({x}_{2}\\,-\\,{x}_{1})\\,+\\,⋯\\,+\\,({x}_{m}\\,+\\,{x}_{m-1})({x}_{m}\\,-\\,{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})+({x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{m-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}}-{x}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}^{2}+{x}_{m}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =(-1)^{2}-(-4)^{2} \\\\  & =-15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we finally arrive at\n\n$$\n-3{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}\\cdot {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}=(-3)\\cdot (-15)\\cdot 1=45.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378115 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f913fab-d0b5-5e9e-b292-039afe4a148c" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Double Sum Over a Rectangular Partition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42fa3e00-e4df-50e3-99c1-d9a7234f86f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378117} {:answer/id #uuid "404c3346-e060-5f84-b07f-a4645328bad5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378118} {:answer/id #uuid "33601d61-2862-53f1-84ba-8845b4beab9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378119} {:answer/id #uuid "ab5d5eae-f7a7-5505-a8b0-1cd83387c69d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378120} {:answer/id #uuid "74d2f886-7603-5112-9981-b3cbff737a08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378